# Tecla -- the keyboard layout viewer. gnome-control-center's Keyboard panel
# launches it from the "View Keyboard Layout" button, so without it that button
# is present and does nothing.
#
# BLFS 12.4, pinned here rather than in versions.env: versions.env is
# regenerated wholesale from the LFS book by tools/pin-versions.sh, so a desktop
# pin placed there is destroyed by the next `make pin`.
SRC_URL=https://download.gnome.org/sources/tecla/48/tecla-48.0.2.tar.xz
SRC_SHA256=783d3464d2a2cf7eb1507649dbd9ff09ce24852c2a6c9a0d365db84063d3d401
SRC_DIR=tecla-48.0.2

# NO OPTIONS AT ALL. This package has no meson_options.txt -- checked rather
# than assumed -- so there is nothing to pin and nothing that can drift with the
# builder image. Recorded because an empty MESON_ARGS in a tree where every
# other recipe carries a paragraph of flags looks like an omission.
#
# Its four dependencies are all hard and all packaged: gtk4, libadwaita-1 >= 1.4,
# xkbcommon, and gtk4-wayland/wayland-client which are taken `required: false`
# and resolve here because this tree's gtk4 has the Wayland backend.
MESON_ARGS=""
